  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23569963.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Pacific Ocean Shelf Tracking (POST) Project Database",
  "description": "The Pacific Ocean Shelf Tracking (POST) project database provides web-based access to data collected through the project. It contains three areas of information: - Receivers: Location, serial numbers, and name of line; - Tags: Identification number, and species and stock of tagged animal; and - Detections: Location, time, tag detected and detecting receiver Researchers can download http://www.meds-sdmm.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/post/databaseInit.do?req=down available data or view products http://www.meds-sdmm.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/post/databaseInit.do?req=product based on uploaded data. Password access is required for the most recent data.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: The Pacific Ocean Shelf Tracking (POST) project aims to build an acoustic tracking array along the west coast of North America. The early applications focused on tracking the migration, life span, movement and behavior of Pacific salmon. The project is expanding to encompass other species such as rockfish, sturgeon and small pelagics.",
